      "extract": "The starting point of the paper [1] was Thurston’s amazing insight in the 1980’s that all 3-dimensional manifolds should be canonically divisible into pieces having a well-defined geometric structure of one of eight types, the most important of which is the hyperbolic one. In conjunction with the famous Mostow rigidity the‐ orem, this means that 3-dimensional topology becomes a part, first of differential geometry,",
